    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7841",
      "problem": "Find the image of the point $(-5,2)$ under the action of a dilation with center $O$ and scale factor $-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "A dilation with center at the origin and a scale factor of $-3$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\mapsto (-3x,-3y).\n$$\n\nApplying this function to the point $(-5,2),$ we have\n\n$$\n(-5,2) \\mapsto \\big((-3) \\cdot (-5), \\: (-3) \\cdot 2 \\big) = (15,-6).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resulting point is $(15,-6).$",
